From 0e8580614a45ab832762437439e11335378df920 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:33:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: rate Tap Unlife at the spell's real damage, not the
 target's full hp

borg_launch_damage_one()'s BORG_ATTACK_TAP_UNLIFE case computed the mana
gain as BI_CURSP - BI_CURSP (always zero) and then rated the cast at
kill->power - sp_drain -- the target's full estimated hp. The comment
above it says to ignore the mana gain. Rate the tap at the passed average
damage like the sibling dispel cases (DISP_UNDEAD, DISP_EVIL), zero for
non-undead, so a free level-7 spell no longer looks like a one-shot for
any undead.
---
 src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c | 5 -----
 1 file changed, 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c b/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c
index 4e1630e6f..8356ffea5 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c
@@ -1104,11 +1104,6 @@ static int borg_launch_damage_one(int i, int dam, int typ, int ammo_location)
         /* for now ignore the gain in sp */
         if (!(rf_has(r_ptr->flags, RF_UNDEAD)))
             dam = 0;
-        else {
-            int sp_drain = borg.trait[BI_CURSP] - borg.trait[BI_CURSP];
-            if (sp_drain < kill->power)
-                dam = kill->power - sp_drain;
-        }
         break;
 
     case BORG_ATTACK_CURSE:
-- 
